{"id":"mahabharata-3-294","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":294,"title":"चतुर्नवत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 294 · Karna gives away his armour","summary":{"en":"Karna offers the disguised Indra cows, women and lands, but Indra asks only for the armour and earrings. Knowing who he is, Karna asks in return for Indra's unfailing spear, which will kill one enemy and then return to Indra; he cuts the armour and earrings from his body, is named Vaikartana, and the Kauravas are dismayed while the Pandavas rejoice.","kn":"ಕರ್ಣನು ವೇಷಧಾರಿ ಇಂದ್ರನಿಗೆ ಗೋವು, ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರು, ಭೂಮಿಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಡಲು ಮುಂದಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಆದರೆ ಇಂದ್ರನು ಕವಚ ಕುಂಡಲಗಳನ್ನು ಮಾತ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವನಾರೆಂದು ತಿಳಿದ ಕರ್ಣನು ಪ್ರತಿಯಾಗಿ ಒಬ್ಬ ಶತ್ರುವನ್ನು ಕೊಂದು ಇಂದ್ರನಿಗೆ ಮರಳುವ ಅಮೋಘ ಶಕ್ತಿಯನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿ, ದೇಹದಿಂದ ಕವಚ ಕುಂಡಲಗಳನ್ನು ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿ ವೈಕರ್ತನನೆನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೌರವರು ಖಿನ್ನರಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಪಾಂಡವರು ಹರ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"कर्ण वेशधारी इन्द्र को गौएँ, स्त्रियाँ और भूमि देने को तैयार होता है, पर इन्द्र केवल कवच-कुण्डल माँगते हैं। उन्हें पहचानकर कर्ण बदले में इन्द्र की अमोघ शक्ति माँगता है, जो एक शत्रु को मारकर इन्द्र के पास लौट जाएगी; वह अपने शरीर से कवच-कुण्डल काटकर वैकर्तन कहलाता है, और कौरव खिन्न होते हैं जबकि पाण्डव हर्षित।","te":"కర్ణుడు వేషధారి ఇంద్రునికి గోవులు, స్త్రీలు, భూములు ఇవ్వడానికి సిద్ధపడతాడు, కానీ ఇంద్రుడు కవచకుండలాలనే అడుగుతాడు. అతడెవరో తెలిసిన కర్ణుడు బదులుగా ఒక శత్రువును చంపి ఇంద్రుని వద్దకు తిరిగివెళ్లే అమోఘమైన శక్తిని కోరి, శరీరం నుండి కవచకుండలాలను కోసి వైకర్తనుడనిపించుకుంటాడు; కౌరవులు నిరాశపడతారు, పాండవులు ఆనందిస్తారు.","ta":"கர்ணன் வேடமிட்ட இந்திரனுக்குப் பசுக்கள், பெண்கள், நிலங்களைத் தர முன்வர, இந்திரன் கவச குண்டலங்களை மட்டுமே கேட்கிறான். அவன் யாரென்று அறிந்த கர்ணன் பதிலாக ஒரு பகைவனைக் கொன்று இந்திரனிடம் திரும்பும் தவறாத சக்தியைக் கேட்டு, உடலிலிருந்து கவச குண்டலங்களை அறுத்து வைகர்த்தனன் எனப் பெயர் பெறுகிறான்; கௌரவர்கள் வருந்த, பாண்டவர்கள் மகிழ்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"ഇന്ദ്രൻ ബ്രാഹ്മണവേഷത്തിൽ വന്നപ്പോൾ കർണ്ണൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് പശുക്കളെയും സ്ത്രീകളെയും ഭൂമിയെയും വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു; പക്ഷേ ഇന്ദ്രൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നത് കവചവും കുണ്ഡലങ്ങളും മാത്രം. ആരാണ് മുന്നിൽ നിൽക്കുന്നതെന്ന് അറിയുന്ന കർണ്ണൻ, പകരമായി ഇന്ദ്രന്റെ പിഴയ്ക്കാത്ത കുന്തം ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; ഒരു ശത്രുവിനെ കൊന്ന് അത് ഇന്ദ്രന്റെ അടുത്തേക്ക് മടങ്ങും; അദ്ദേഹം ശരീരത്തിൽനിന്ന് കവചവും കുണ്ഡലങ്ങളും മുറിച്ചെടുക്കുന്നു, വൈകർത്തനൻ എന്ന് വിളിക്കപ്പെടുന്നു; കൗരവർ ദുഃഖിക്കുമ്പോൾ പാണ്ഡവർ സന്തോഷിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.294; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कुण्डलाहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Kundalaharana Parva (Taking of the earrings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"देवराजमनुप्राप्तं ब्राह्मणच्छद्मना वृषः ।\nदृष्ट्वा स्वागतमित्याह न बुबोधास्य मानसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the king of the gods arrived in the guise of a brahmin, Vrisha said, Welcome, and did not perceive his mind."}},{"n":2,"text":"हिरण्यकण्ठीः प्रमदा ग्रामान्वा बहुगोकुलान् ।\nकिं ददानीति तं विप्रमुवाचाधिरथिस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Adhiratha's son said to the brahmin: Shall I give you gold-necklaced women, or villages with many herds of cows?"}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"हिरण्यकण्ठ्यः प्रमदा यच्चान्यत्प्रीतिवर्धनम् ।\nनाहं दत्तमिहेच्छामि तदर्थिभ्यः प्रदीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gold-necklaced women and whatever else increases delight, I do not want what is given here; give those to others who ask for them."}},{"n":4,"text":"यदेतत्सहजं वर्म कुण्डले च तवानघ ।\nएतदुत्कृत्य मे देहि यदि सत्यव्रतो भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This natural armor and these earrings of yours, blameless one: cut them off and give them to me, if you are true to your vow."}},{"n":5,"text":"एतदिच्छाम्यहं क्षिप्रं त्वया दत्तं परंतप ।\nएष मे सर्वलाभानां लाभः परमको मतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I want this given by you quickly, scorcher of foes; I consider this the best of all gains for me."}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"अवनिं प्रमदा गाश्च निर्वापं बहुवार्षिकम् ।\nतत्ते विप्र प्रदास्यामि न तु वर्म न कुण्डले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Land, women, cows, and food enough for many years I will give you, brahmin, but not the armor and the earrings."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"एवं बहुविधैर्वाक्यैर्याच्यमानः स तु द्विजः ।\nकर्णेन भरतश्रेष्ठ नान्यं वरमयाचत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though Karna pleaded with him with many kinds of words, best of Bharatas, the brahmin asked for no other boon."}},{"n":8,"text":"सान्त्वितश्च यथाशक्ति पूजितश्च यथाविधि ।\nनैवान्यं स द्विजश्रेष्ठः कामयामास वै वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Comforted as far as possible and honored properly, the best of brahmins still wished for no other boon."}},{"n":9,"text":"यदा नान्यं प्रवृणुते वरं वै द्विजसत्तमः ।\nतदैनमब्रवीद्भूयो राधेयः प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the best of brahmins would choose no other boon, the son of Radha said to him once more, as if laughing:"}},{"n":10,"text":"सहजं वर्म मे विप्र कुण्डले चामृतोद्भवे ।\nतेनावध्योऽस्मि लोकेषु ततो नैतद्ददाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My armor is innate, brahmin, and the earrings were born of nectar; by them I cannot be killed in the worlds, so I do not give them."}},{"n":11,"text":"विशालं पृथिवीराज्यं क्षेमं निहतकण्टकम् ।\nप्रतिगृह्णीष्व मत्तस्त्वं साधु ब्राह्मणपुंगव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take from me instead a vast kingdom of the earth, secure and with thorns removed, bull among brahmins."}},{"n":12,"text":"कुण्डलाभ्यां विमुक्तोऽहं वर्मणा सहजेन च ।\nगमनीयो भविष्यामि शत्रूणां द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deprived of the earrings and my natural armor, best of brahmins, I would become easy prey for my enemies."}},{"n":13,"text":"यदा नान्यं वरं वव्रे भगवान्पाकशासनः ।\nततः प्रहस्य कर्णस्तं पुनरित्यब्रवीद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the lord Indra chose no other boon, Karna laughed and again spoke to him:"}},{"n":14,"text":"विदितो देवदेवेश प्रागेवासि मम प्रभो ।\nन तु न्याय्यं मया दातुं तव शक्र वृथा वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, god of gods, I knew you before; but it is not right for me to give you, Indra, a boon in vain."}},{"n":15,"text":"त्वं हि देवेश्वरः साक्षात्त्वया देयो वरो मम ।\nअन्येषां चैव भूतानामीश्वरो ह्यसि भूतकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are indeed the lord of the gods; you should give me a boon. You are lord of other beings too, and their maker."}},{"n":16,"text":"यदि दास्यामि ते देव कुण्डले कवचं तथा ।\nवध्यतामुपयास्यामि त्वं च शक्रावहास्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I give you the earrings and armor, god, I shall become killable, and you, Indra, would be laughed at."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्माद्विनिमयं कृत्वा कुण्डले वर्म चोत्तमम् ।\nहरस्व शक्र कामं मे न दद्यामहमन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"So make an exchange, Indra, and take the earrings and the excellent armor as you wish; otherwise I will not give them."}},{"text":"शक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"विदितोऽहं रवेः पूर्वमायन्नेव तवान्तिकम् ।\nतेन ते सर्वमाख्यातमेवमेतन्न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I was made known to you beforehand by Surya as I was coming to you; he told you everything, no doubt."}},{"n":19,"text":"काममस्तु तथा तात तव कर्ण यथेच्छसि ।\nवर्जयित्वा तु मे वज्रं प्रवृणीष्व यदिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let it be as you wish, dear Karna; except for my thunderbolt, choose whatever you want."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः कर्णः प्रहृष्टस्तु उपसंगम्य वासवम् ।\nअमोघां शक्तिमभ्येत्य वव्रे संपूर्णमानसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna, delighted, approached Indra and, with a fully satisfied mind, chose the unfailing spear."}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"वर्मणा कुण्डलाभ्यां च शक्तिं मे देहि वासव ।\nअमोघां शत्रुसंघानां घातनीं पृतनामुखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In exchange for the armor and earrings, Indra, give me your unfailing spear, which kills hordes of enemies at the head of an army."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"ततः संचिन्त्य मनसा मुहूर्तमिव वासवः ।\nशक्त्यर्थं पृथिवीपाल कर्णं वाक्यमथाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, thinking it over in his mind for a moment, Indra, lord of the earth, said to Karna concerning the spear:"}},{"n":23,"text":"कुण्डले मे प्रयच्छस्व वर्म चैव शरीरजम् ।\nगृहाण कर्ण शक्तिं त्वमनेन समयेन मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give me the earrings and the armor that grew with your body, Karna, and take the spear on this condition."}},{"n":24,"text":"अमोघा हन्ति शतशः शत्रून्मम करच्युता ।\nपुनश्च पाणिमभ्येति मम दैत्यान्विनिघ्नतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unfailing, when released from my hand it kills hundreds of enemies, and it returns to my hand as I slay the Daityas."}},{"n":25,"text":"सेयं तव करं प्राप्य हत्वैकं रिपुमूर्जितम् ।\nगर्जन्तं प्रतपन्तं च मामेवैष्यति सूतज ॥","meaning":{"en":"When it reaches your hand, charioteer's son, it will kill one powerful enemy, one who roars and blazes, and then come back to me."}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"एकमेवाहमिच्छामि रिपुं हन्तुं महाहवे ।\nगर्जन्तं प्रतपन्तं च यतो मम भयं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I want to kill just one enemy in the great battle, the one who roars and blazes, from whom I have fear."}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"एकं हनिष्यसि रिपुं गर्जन्तं बलिनं रणे ।\nत्वं तु यं प्रार्थयस्येकं रक्ष्यते स महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will kill one mighty enemy who roars in battle; but the one you seek is guarded by the great one."}},{"n":28,"text":"यमाहुर्वेदविद्वांसो वराहमजितं हरिम् ।\nनारायणमचिन्त्यं च तेन कृष्णेन रक्ष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whom the knowers of the Vedas call the unconquered Boar, Hari, the inconceivable Narayana, by him, Krishna, he is protected."}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"एवमप्यस्तु भगवन्नेकवीरवधे मम ।\nअमोघा प्रवरा शक्तिर्येन हन्यां प्रतापिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even so, lord, let it be, for the killing of one hero; the supreme unfailing spear will kill the mighty one."}},{"n":30,"text":"उत्कृत्य तु प्रदास्यामि कुण्डले कवचं च ते ।\nनिकृत्तेषु च गात्रेषु न मे बीभत्सता भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will cut off and give you the earrings and the armor, and when my limbs are cut, let there be no ugliness in me."}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"न ते बीभत्सता कर्ण भविष्यति कथंचन ।\nव्रणश्चापि न गात्रेषु यस्त्वं नानृतमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"There will be no ugliness in you, Karna, and no wound on your limbs, since you do not wish for falsehood."}},{"n":32,"text":"यादृशस्ते पितुर्वर्णस्तेजश्च वदतां वर ।\nतादृशेनैव वर्णेन त्वं कर्ण भविता पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of speakers, you will have again the same color and brightness as your father had."}},{"n":33,"text":"विद्यमानेषु शस्त्रेषु यद्यमोघामसंशये ।\nप्रमत्तो मोक्ष्यसे चापि त्वय्येवैषा पतिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, while other weapons are available, you carelessly release the unfailing spear, it will fall on you yourself, without doubt."}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":34,"text":"संशयं परमं प्राप्य विमोक्ष्ये वासवीमिमाम् ।\nयथा मामात्थ शक्र त्वं सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will release Indra's spear only when in extreme danger; as you tell me, Indra, I say this truly."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"ततः शक्तिं प्रज्वलितां प्रतिगृह्य विशां पते ।\nशस्त्रं गृहीत्वा निशितं सर्वगात्राण्यकृन्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of men, taking the blazing spear and a sharp weapon, he cut off the armor from all his limbs."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततो देवा मानवा दानवाश्च\nनिकृन्तन्तं कर्णमात्मानमेवम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा सर्वे सिद्धसंघाश्च नेदु-\nर्न ह्यस्यासीद्दुःखजो वै विकारः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Karna thus cutting himself, gods, humans, Danavas and hosts of Siddhas all cried out, but he showed no change from pain."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततो दिव्या दुन्दुभयः प्रणेदुः\nपपातोच्चैः पुष्पवर्षं च दिव्यम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा कर्णं शस्त्रसंकृत्तगात्रं\nमुहुश्चापि स्मयमानं नृवीरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then divine drums sounded and a divine shower of flowers fell, as they saw Karna, hero among men, his limbs cut by the blade, smiling again and again."}},{"n":38,"text":"ततश्छित्त्वा कवचं दिव्यमङ्गा-\nत्तथैवार्द्रं प्रददौ वासवाय ।\nतथोत्कृत्य प्रददौ कुण्डले ते\nवैकर्तनः कर्मणा तेन कर्णः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, cutting the divine armor from his body, still moist, he gave it to Indra; and likewise Karna Vaikartana cut out the earrings and gave them, by that deed."}},{"n":39,"text":"ततः शक्रः प्रहसन्वञ्चयित्वा\nकर्णं लोके यशसा योजयित्वा ।\nकृतं कार्यं पाण्डवानां हि मेने\nततः पश्चाद्दिवमेवोत्पपात ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Indra, laughing, having deceived Karna yet joined him to fame in the world, thought the Pandavas' task done, and rose to heaven."}},{"n":40,"text":"श्रुत्वा कर्णं मुषितं धार्तराष्ट्रा\nदीनाः सर्वे भग्नदर्पा इवासन् ।\nतां चावस्थां गमितं सूतपुत्रं\nश्रुत्वा पार्था जहृषुः काननस्थाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that Karna was robbed, Dhritarashtra's sons were all downcast, their pride broken; but hearing the charioteer's son brought to that state, the Parthas in the forest rejoiced."}},{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"क्वस्था वीराः पाण्डवास्ते बभूवुः\nकुतश्चैतच्छ्रुतवन्तः प्रियं ते ।\nकिं वाकार्षुर्द्वादशेऽब्दे व्यतीते\nतन्मे सर्वं भगवान्व्याकरोतु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where were the heroic Pandavas then, and from where did they hear this welcome news? And what did they do when the twelfth year had passed? Let the lord tell me all."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":42,"text":"लब्ध्वा कृष्णां सैन्धवं द्रावयित्वा\nविप्रैः सार्धं काम्यकादाश्रमात्ते ।\nमार्कण्डेयाच्छ्रुतवन्तः पुराणं\nदेवर्षीणां चरितं विस्तरेण ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gained Krishna and routed the Sindhu king, they, with the brahmins, left the Kamyaka hermitage, having heard from Markandeya the ancient history of the divine sages in detail."}},{"n":43,"text":"प्रत्याजग्मुः सरथाः सानुयात्राः\nसर्वैः सार्धं सूदपौरोगवैश्च ।\nततः पुण्यं द्वैतवनं नृवीरा\nनिस्तीर्योग्रं वनवासं समग्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With chariots and attendants, with all the cooks and the leading men, they returned to the holy Dvaita forest, those heroes among men, having crossed their entire harsh forest exile."}}]}]}